{"kind":"artifact","text":"One mermaid flowchart added to docs/how-to/keep-decision-records.md at exact clean pushed head cf9fc676a20a7ed33d657b617fa4d040a98c1ee7 on request/decision-records-flowchart, cut from current main. One file, +36 lines, nothing removed and no prose changed.\n\nIt is one diagram, as the request required, and it kept actor attribution -- author, ratifier, reviewer are named on the steps where they act. I did not have to trade attribution for legibility, so the fallback planner authorised was not needed.\n\nPlacement is line 31, ahead of Setup at 64 and the first step at 85, so a reader meets the shape before the ceremony rather than after 321 lines of it. The dialect follows docs/reference/architecture.md line 34: flowchart TB, a subgraph, br line breaks.\n\nThe fact the request called the point of the exercise is carried explicitly rather than implied by arrow direction. The adoption node reads \"the ratifier ratifies the proposal -- never the artifact\", and the request node reads \"Review request -- after adoption\". Those are the two things a reader gets wrong, so they are words in the boxes rather than something to infer.\n\nOne correction to the request conditions, which asked that the diagram show \"the verdict resting on artifact and ratified proposal\". The page does not say that and the diagram does not either, because it is not what happens. Line 150 says the REQUEST rests on both the artifact and the ratified proposal, and lines 141-144 say the verdict, the merge receipt and the merged record all reach the adoption through that one chain. So the verdict rests on the request, and reaches adoption transitively. The diagram draws Adopted to Request to Verdict for exactly that reason. I checked the prose rather than encoding the condition, because encoding it would have put a false edge in a picture whose job is to stop people getting this wrong.\n\nGates at this exact head: git diff --check exit 0, go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... exit 0, ok in 65.0s uncached. The mermaid fence is inert to that gate -- docset records the fence info string lowercased as Lang (docset.go:43-44, :215) and examples_test.go runs a block only when Lang is exactly sh (:66, :91) -- which I verified at source rather than assuming.","body":{"commit":"cf9fc676a20a7ed33d657b617fa4d040a98c1ee7","path":"docs/how-to/keep-decision-records.md"}}